# Ships manifest — what of getff's OWN items reaches a consumer, per channel (one-button point 13).
# TAB-delimited, one row per item, same parser contract as companions.manifest (single TAB, no padding):
#   kind<TAB>name<TAB>verdict<TAB>installer<TAB>plugin<TAB>reason
# kind      skill | hook | rule | agent | setting | mcp
#           population (scripts/check-ships-manifest.mjs enumerates it from git):
#             skill   = dirs with SKILL.md under skills/, .claude/skills/, plugin/skills/
#             hook    = .claude/hooks/*.sh + the names plugin/hooks/hooks.json registers
#             rule    = .claude/rules/*.md
#             agent   = agents/*.md + plugin/agents/*.md
#             setting = getff's .claude/settings.json keys (object values expanded one level:
#                       env.<KEY>, permissions.<KEY>); `hooks` is one row — each hook has its own
#             mcp     = getff's .mcp.json mcpServers
# verdict   ships | internal
# installer core | env | factory | full | ask | no — the LOWEST install depth that delivers the item
#           (core ⊂ env ⊂ factory; full = only under -y / --full; ask = a setting that changes how
#           sessions run, written only on the pre-launch «yes» into .claude/settings.local.json with
#           a one-command undo — its value lives in setup.d/session-settings.json, and every key
#           there must be an `ask` row). Checked by a real install:
#           tests/install-sh/ships-manifest.test.sh.
# plugin    yes | no — the Claude Code plugin under plugin/ carries it (checked from the plugin tree).
# reason    `-` or free text (no TAB). Required, >= 20 chars after its prefix, when:
#           internal            → must start «internal, because »; installer must be `no`.
#           internal, plugin=yes → must ALSO carry «plugin copy: <what happens / who removes it>»:
#                                  the plugin ships an item getff calls internal — a known
#                                  contradiction, named, not silent.
#           ships, installer=no, plugin=no → must start «pending: » (who delivers it, and when).
#           installer=factory|full → why the default run (env) does not install it (C1).
#           installer=ask       → what the setting changes for the person.
#           ships, installer=no, plugin=yes → why only the plugin carries it.
# A population item with no row, or a row with no item, fails the check (pre-commit + CI).
skill	getff	ships	core	yes	-
skill	tool-bootstrapping	ships	core	yes	-
skill	template-audit	ships	core	yes	-
skill	ai-doc	ships	core	yes	-
skill	rule-research	ships	core	yes	-
skill	rule-tests	ships	core	yes	-
skill	arch	ships	env	no	-
skill	night-mode	ships	env	no	-
skill	orchestrator	ships	env	no	-
skill	pipeline	ships	env	no	-
skill	reviewer	ships	env	no	-
skill	dispatcher	ships	factory	no	presupposes the aif-handoff runtime; without it its triggers fire into a dead end. The one button installs it through --all when aif answers /health (setup.d/10-skills.sh:113-131)
skill	aif-doctor	ships	factory	no	presupposes the aif-handoff runtime; without it its triggers fire into a dead end. The one button installs it through --all when aif answers /health (setup.d/10-skills.sh:113-131)
skill	harvest	ships	factory	no	presupposes the aif-handoff runtime; without it its triggers fire into a dead end. The one button installs it through --all when aif answers /health (setup.d/10-skills.sh:113-131)
skill	claude-glm-executor-handoff	ships	factory	no	presupposes the aif-handoff runtime; without it its triggers fire into a dead end. The one button installs it through --all when aif answers /health (setup.d/10-skills.sh:113-131)
skill	story	ships	factory	no	no runtime reason: the operator product call of 2026-09-11 keeps it factory-only (setup.d/10-skills.sh:119-123); the report lists it as not installed by the default run
skill	self-reflection	internal	no	no	internal, because it is the §1.7 PR self-review discipline of getff's own development process, not a consumer capability
skill	docs-author	internal	no	no	internal, because it writes pages of the getff.ai site under docs/site/ (scripts/docs-check.mjs:83 binds it to that tree)
skill	using-getff	ships	no	yes	plugin entry point: tells a plugin session how to find the getff skills; an installer consumer reads AGENTS.md and the installed skills instead
skill	installing-enforcement	ships	no	yes	plugin-only bridge to the installer: wires the hard layer for a plugin user; an installer run IS that wiring, so it has nothing to do there
hook	ask-question-reminder	ships	core	yes	-
hook	check-doc-authority-header	ships	core	yes	-
hook	deps-hash-check	ships	core	yes	-
hook	end-of-turn-reminder	ships	core	yes	-
hook	inject-matching-rule	ships	core	yes	-
hook	inject-memory-codification	ships	core	yes	-
hook	inject-output-language	ships	core	yes	-
hook	inject-project-digest	ships	core	yes	-
hook	runtime-bridge-dispatch	ships	factory	yes	dispatches work into the aif-handoff runtime through the vendored runtime bridge, which only a factory install carries
hook	inject-session-bootstrap	internal	no	no	internal, because it injects getff's own goal and invariants into the session
hook	check-doc-authority	internal	no	yes	internal, because it needs getff's principle-09 CLI shim and is a no-op with a getff-specific notice elsewhere; plugin copy: flagged to the plugin/project hook dedup work (plan §1.2), P3 does not edit plugin/hooks/hooks.json
hook	validate-prompt	internal	no	yes	internal, because it validates getff kickoff batch-specs through packages/core/spec-validation; plugin copy: flagged to the plugin/project hook dedup work (plan §1.2), P3 does not edit plugin/hooks/hooks.json
hook	check-worker-dispatch-channel	internal	no	yes	internal, because it needs getff's principle-29 bin and checks getff kickoff dispatch channels; plugin copy: flagged to the plugin/project hook dedup work (plan §1.2), P3 does not edit plugin/hooks/hooks.json
hook	check-kickoff-traps	internal	no	yes	internal, because it enforces getff kickoff conventions by getff principle numbers; plugin copy: flagged to the plugin/project hook dedup work (plan §1.2), P3 does not edit plugin/hooks/hooks.json
hook	check-hook-marker	internal	no	yes	internal, because it checks getff's @dual-pair hook markers and skips when dual-implementation-discipline.md is absent; plugin copy: flagged to the plugin/project hook dedup work (plan §1.2), P3 does not edit plugin/hooks/hooks.json
hook	inject-subagent-context	ships	no	yes	ZCode fallback: exits unless ZCODE_PROJECT_DIR is set; the installer targets Claude Code, which has its own subagent context channel
hook	inject-subagent-digest	internal	no	no	internal, because it sends getff's own session digest to subagents; consumers get inject-project-digest instead
hook	close-aif-task-on-merge	internal	no	no	internal, because it closes aif tasks through packages/runtime-bridge harvest.ts, which no install vendors
hook	inject-handoff-on-compact	ships	env	no	installer-only: env+ installs it with the handoff group (setup.d/10-skills.sh §1k); no plugin copy, because the handoff it injects is kept only under the AIF_HANDOFF_GATE ask row, which only the installer offers, and the plugin SessionStart slot is taken (the harness renderer lists it in PLUGIN_INCOMPATIBLE)
hook	precompact-residue	ships	env	no	installer-only: env+ installs it with the handoff group (setup.d/10-skills.sh §1k) beside its reader inject-handoff-on-compact; the group ships through the installer only, and a plugin copy is one of the follow-ons the premise-7 addendum of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-08-handoff-currency-gate-design.md reopens, not decided here
hook	warn-subagent-report	internal	no	no	internal, because the REPORT block format it checks is a getff delegation convention
hook	warn-subagent-report-zcode	ships	no	yes	ZCode variant of the subagent report check, carried only by the plugin (the ZCode channel); flagged to the hook dedup work with its Claude Code sibling
hook	session-start	ships	no	yes	plugin bootstrap: announces the plugin skills at session start; an installer consumer gets AGENTS.md and inject-project-digest instead
hook	glossary-inject	internal	no	no	internal, because it reads CONTEXT.md, getff's own glossary, which no install ships; registered nowhere
hook	adopt-orchestrator-prompts	internal	no	no	internal, because it adopts files into getff's own .claude/orchestrator-prompts store; registered nowhere
hook	worktree-setup	internal	no	no	internal, because WorktreeCreate is not registered even in getff (CLAUDE.md), and its output names getff paths
rule	00-rule-index	internal	no	no	internal, because it is the generated index of getff's own rule set (scripts/render-rule-index.mjs)
rule	ai-laziness-digest	internal	no	no	internal, because it is getff's always-on digest of ai-laziness-traps, which is what ships; principle 35 keeps the two in sync inside getff only
