agent	dispatch-input-checker	internal	no	no	internal, because it is getff's authoring-only dispatch-input reality check station (arch-v2 S-B)
agent	getff-cold-run-prober	internal	no	no	internal, because getff runs it against a consumer; it is not run inside one (spec §9.3)
setting	hooks	ships	core	no	-
setting	autoCompactWindow	ships	ask	no	auto-compacts at 400k tokens instead of the harness default; offered in the pre-launch list, written to .claude/settings.local.json with a one-command undo (setup.d/session-settings.sh)
setting	env.AIF_CTX_WINDOW	internal	no	no	internal, because 1000000 is already the shipped end-of-turn hook's default (.claude/hooks/end-of-turn-reminder.sh:299), and a declared value overrides the window the hook observes (:394-412), which would hide a smaller real window from a consumer
setting	env.CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS	ships	ask	no	turns on the experimental agent-teams feature, which changes how sessions run; offered in the pre-launch list, written to .claude/settings.local.json with a one-command undo
setting	permissions.allow	ships	ask	no	a subset: Task and Agent only; the two hook-path allows are getff operator conveniences for its own hook scripts; offered in the pre-launch list
setting	permissions.deny	ships	ask	no	a subset: the generic destructive-command denies; the four main/master push denies stay out because they encode getff's staging-first flow, not a consumer's; offered in the pre-launch list
setting	env.AIF_HANDOFF_GATE	ships	ask	no	arms the handoff gate, which blocks a turn in the band before compaction until the session handoff is current; offered in the pre-launch list (the two handoff hooks ship at env and are passive without it)
setting	claudeMdExcludes	internal	no	no	internal, because every entry is a path of one of getff's own rule files
mcp	context7	ships	full	no	written to the project .mcp.json only under -y / --full (setup.d/05-mcp.sh); the python lane writes it on every run
mcp	deepwiki	ships	full	no	written to the project .mcp.json under -y / --full only when not configured machine-wide; --global installs it at user scope instead
